{"timestamp_edt": "2026-09-17 10:03:17 EDT", "action_type": "query", "duration_seconds": 6.722983, "file_name": "", "query_text": "What role did Caesar Russell serve in Captain William North's company?", "steps_taken": [{"step": "embed query", "seconds": 2.890329}, {"step": "keyword extraction", "seconds": 0.000327}, {"step": "vector retrieval", "seconds": 0.141043}, {"step": "context assembly", "seconds": 1e-06}, {"step": "llm answer generation", "seconds": 3.690132}], "tools_called": ["RetrievalService.search_similar_chunks", "RetrievalService.search_ancestry_data"], "api_calls_made": ["embedding (ollama)", "llm (deepseek)"], "final_response": "Caesar Russell served as the “personal servant” to Captain William North, who was an aide-de-camp to General Friedrich Wilhelm August Heinrich Ferdinand von Steuben [Document 1].", "response_time_seconds": 3.690132, "input_tokens": 834, "output_tokens": 125, "input_cache_hit_tokens": 128, "input_cache_miss_tokens": 706, "estimated_cost_usd": 0.000716, "pricing_rate": "off-peak", "reasoning_mode": "low"}
{"timestamp_edt": "2026-09-17 10:05:12 EDT", "action_type": "query", "duration_seconds": 11.227075, "file_name": "", "query_text": "What ship did Caesar Russell sail on to Calcutta, and when did it depart?", "steps_taken": [{"step": "embed query", "seconds": 2.151129}, {"step": "keyword extraction", "seconds": 0.000925}, {"step": "vector retrieval", "seconds": 0.284697}, {"step": "context assembly", "seconds": 2e-06}, {"step": "llm answer generation", "seconds": 8.789437}], "tools_called": ["RetrievalService.search_similar_chunks", "RetrievalService.search_ancestry_data"], "api_calls_made": ["embedding (ollama)", "llm (deepseek)"], "final_response": "Caesar Russell sailed to Calcutta, India, aboard the **Friendship of Salem**, a full-rigged ship of 342 tons [footnote 116]. He was listed as cook, age 41, height 5’4”, birthplace Middleton, residence Salem [Document 2][footnote 107]. The crew list shows two departure dates associated with this voyage from Salem: **06 Mar 1806** and **08 Mar 1806** [Document 2]. The Friendship of Salem’s voyages are also documented by the National Park Service at Salem Maritime National Historic Site [footnote 110].", "response_time_seconds": 8.789437, "input_tokens": 4671, "output_tokens": 513, "input_cache_hit_tokens": 128, "input_cache_miss_tokens": 4543, "estimated_cost_usd": 0.004017, "pricing_rate": "off-peak", "reasoning_mode": "low"}
{"timestamp_edt": "2026-09-17 10:06:10 EDT", "action_type": "query", "duration_seconds": 7.156175, "file_name": "", "query_text": "Where was Tobias Hill born, and on what date?", "steps_taken": [{"step": "embed query", "seconds": 2.111041}, {"step": "keyword extraction", "seconds": 0.000233}, {"step": "vector retrieval", "seconds": 0.235539}, {"step": "context assembly", "seconds": 1e-06}, {"step": "llm answer generation", "seconds": 4.808603}], "tools_called": ["RetrievalService.search_similar_chunks", "RetrievalService.search_ancestry_data"], "api_calls_made": ["embedding (ollama)", "llm (deepseek)"], "final_response": "Tobias Hill was born on November 18, 1743, in rural Georgetown, Maine [335]. He was born to Sandusky and Peggy (also recorded as Margaret) Hill [Document 4, Document 8]. The earliest record of the Hill family appears in the Vital Records of Georgetown, Maine, where first-born Tobias is listed as “Jobe,” likely a transcription error of “Tobe” [335].", "response_time_seconds": 4.808603, "input_tokens": 3094, "output_tokens": 270, "input_cache_hit_tokens": 128, "input_cache_miss_tokens": 2966, "estimated_cost_usd": 0.002495, "pricing_rate": "off-peak", "reasoning_mode": "low"}
{"timestamp_edt": "2026-09-17 10:09:42 EDT", "action_type": "query", "duration_seconds": 12.405868, "file_name": "", "query_text": "Was Tobias Hill's brother Richard Hill the same person as Richard Denny in Revolutionary War records?", "steps_taken": [{"step": "embed query", "seconds": 2.129934}, {"step": "keyword extraction", "seconds": 0.000281}, {"step": "vector retrieval", "seconds": 0.342603}, {"step": "context assembly", "seconds": 2.3e-05}, {"step": "llm answer generation", "seconds": 9.932344}], "tools_called": ["RetrievalService.search_similar_chunks", "RetrievalService.search_ancestry_data"], "api_calls_made": ["embedding (ollama)", "llm (deepseek)"], "final_response": "The provided context does not explicitly confirm that Richard Hill and Richard Denny were the same person. Document 1 states: “There is evidence that Tobias’ brother Richard separated from the Hill family at the age of five and also served in the Revolutionary War. Tobias Hill's brother (Dick/Richard) was sold to Daniel Denny in 1752, and later willed to Daniel Denny's son Samuel in 1761.” It further notes: “There are Revolutionary War records for both Richard Hill and Richard Denny in Leicester, Worcester, MA. Both are identified as Negro,” and that a Massachusetts Archive Archivist observed “a lot of overlap between these two men (both from Leicester, served in Capt. Brown’s Company).” However, the documents describe this as overlap and evidence, not as a definitive identification that the two names refer to one individual.", "response_time_seconds": 9.932344, "input_tokens": 3049, "output_tokens": 616, "input_cache_hit_tokens": 128, "input_cache_miss_tokens": 2921, "estimated_cost_usd": 0.00315, "pricing_rate": "off-peak", "reasoning_mode": "low"}
{"timestamp_edt": "2026-09-17 10:56:09 EDT", "action_type": "query", "duration_seconds": 24.175019, "file_name": "", "query_text": "When was J.Perkins born?", "steps_taken": [{"step": "embed query", "seconds": 2.615843}, {"step": "keyword extraction", "seconds": 0.00033}, {"step": "vector retrieval", "seconds": 0.444852}, {"step": "context assembly", "seconds": 3e-06}, {"step": "llm answer generation", "seconds": 21.112743}], "tools_called": ["RetrievalService.search_similar_chunks", "RetrievalService.search_ancestry_data"], "api_calls_made": ["embedding (ollama)", "llm (deepseek)"], "final_response": "Based on the documents, Joshua “Old Jock” Perkins was born about 1732 in Accomack County, Virginia [Document 5; Document 7]. If you are asking about Jacob Perkins, the documents do not provide an exact birth date, but he was described as “aged two years” around 1748, which suggests he was born approximately 1746 [Document 3, footnote 28].", "response_time_seconds": 21.112743, "input_tokens": 4227, "output_tokens": 1395, "input_cache_hit_tokens": 128, "input_cache_miss_tokens": 4099, "estimated_cost_usd": 0.00547, "pricing_rate": "off-peak", "reasoning_mode": "low"}
